"""Zoo 1.115.0: a desk's computer is on (the factory's roadmap 148).

The walker's look review, 2026-10-19: "computer screens hsould be on...bring life to this dead world". Every monitor
on every desk and cubicle bank showed the dark `screen` finish.

What it changes (anchored; each file pinned by hash; nothing written on a miss):
  * zoo_keeper/core/desk_screens.py (new) -- six invented 1997 office screens, painted in pure Python.
  * zoo_keeper/recipes/_surface_stock.py -- a monitor carries an art quad 2.5 mm in front of its glass, which an
    item's footprint ignores; `plan_surface` names its app from where the monitor stands and asks for every app's
    tile.
  * zoo_keeper/core/card_art.py -- `paint` dispatches a `desk_screen` tile.
  * zoo_keeper/bpylayer/prim_mesh.py -- `build_stock` builds the screens on a backlit `M_StockScreen_<atlas>_Face`.
  * tests/test_desk_screens.py (new) -- 74.
  * tests/test_flat_art.py -- finding 5's test names the office as the other flavour that plans tiles.
  * VERSION 1.114.1 -> 1.115.0, CHANGELOG.

Generated by `patches/zoo_desk_screens/gen_zoo_desk_screens.py` from a proven clone; its dry runs, the kit A/B and
the suites are beside it.

    python patches/patch_zoo_desk_screens.py
"""
